//
// THE CELL THAT MOST HAD TO BE REACHED (loft#1103, the narrow half of
// `1103b-a-nullable-branch-arm-refused.loft`).  `types.md` keeps `(N-Store)` a hard ERROR for
// u8…u32 because "the null would collide with a real value" — the sentinel is a real `u8`, so
// a null in a non-null narrow slot cannot be told from `255`.  Every other branch-arm cell is
// recoverable with a warning by the rule; this one is not, and it was reachable through an
// else arm.  Its own file because an error stops a file before it runs, and the other cells
// now run.
//
// @falsified-at: 8498fdf1 → here (hand-measured): the parent build refuses it with a
//   different text (`cannot change type from integer(0, 255) to integer(0, 255)?`).
//   HOLDS: on --interpret, assertions, leak, panic, free-refusal are equal on both trees,
//   measured by `scripts/falsify.sh --bulk` against 8498fdf1; falsify prints only the
//   channels that MOVE, and requires HERE to be clean, so each of those is clean on both. The
//   exit/expectations channel carries this one on that backend. The native side was not
//   scored in that run.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: a nullable `integer(0, 255)?` cannot be stored into the local `x` of the non-null type `integer(0, 255)`
fn maybe_u8_1103c(k: integer) -> u8? { if k > 5 { 7 as u8 } else { null } }

fn test_a_narrow_width_arm_is_refused() {
  k = 1;
  x: u8 = if k == 9 { 1 as u8 } else { maybe_u8_1103c(k) };
  assert(x as integer == 1, "unreachable — the declaration above is refused");
}
